# SUBSEA Part 1

The SUBSEA Part 1 expedition aboard the R/V *Falkor* (too) explored connections between upper ocean productivity, nutrient cycling, and carbon export across the subtropical South Atlantic. Over 35 days at sea, the team conducted continuous interdisciplinary observations using CTD systems, sediment traps, autonomous vehicles, productivity arrays, in situ pumps, and shipboard experiments.

This page collects expedition updates, videos, and photography from the cruise.

