## About SUBSEA

SUBSEA (Subtropical Underwater Biogeochemistry and Subsurface Export Alliance) is an international research collaboration focused on understanding how biological and chemical processes regulate carbon export and nutrient cycling in the subtropical ocean. The expedition was conducted aboard the Schmidt Ocean Institute research vessel R/V *Falkor* (too) as part of the Ocean Biogeochemistry Virtual Institute (OBVI).
